## Starting {{ provisioner_name }}

Starting {{ provisioner_name }} can take a while especially when the node images
are being downloaded for the first time. The status of all {{ provisioner_name
}} services can be checked with:

```bash
systemctl list-dependencies openchami.target
```

By default the cloud-init server keeps its groups and defaults in memory, so
they are lost whenever its container restarts. This drop-in for its quadlet
stores them in a database file on its `cloud-init-data` volume instead:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Keep cloud-init data across restarts -->
```bash
mkdir -p /etc/containers/systemd/cloud-init-server.container.d
cat > /etc/containers/systemd/cloud-init-server.container.d/ohpc-storage.conf <<EOF
[Container]
Environment=STORAGE_BACKEND=quack
Environment=DB_PATH=/cloud-init/cloud-init.db
EOF
systemctl daemon-reload
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Starting OpenCHAMI -->
```bash
systemctl enable --now openchami.target
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
